?><!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"><title>Disaster Recovery - Healthcare Wellness Club</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/dashboard.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/step10.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/product_pro.css"></head><body><header class="os-topbar"><div class="os-topbar-inner"><a class="os-brand" href="backup_center.php"><img src="../img/logo.png" alt="logo"><span><strong>Healthcare Wellness Club</strong><small>STEP 18 • Disaster Recovery Runbook</small></span></a><div class="os-top-actions"><a class="os-btn" href="backup_restore.php">Restore</a><a class="os-btn" href="cloud_readiness.php">Cloud</a><a class="os-btn primary" href="backup_center.php">Backup Center</a></div></div></header><div class="os-layout"><aside class="os-sidebar"><div class="os-nav-label">Recovery</div><nav class="os-nav"><a href="backup_center.php"><i class="dot"></i>Backup Center</a><a href="backup_history.php"><i class="dot"></i>Backup History</a><a href="backup_restore.php"><i class="dot"></i>Restore</a><a class="active" href="disaster_recovery.php"><i class="dot"></i>Recovery Runbook</a><a href="cloud_readiness.php"><i class="dot"></i>Cloud Readiness</a><a href="step18_audit.php"><i class="dot"></i>STEP 18 Audit</a></nav></aside><main class="os-main"><section class="os-hero s10-hero"><div class="os-kicker">RECOVER IN A KNOWN ORDER</div><h1>A recovery plan is part of the backup, not an afterthought.</h1><p>This runbook separates emergency containment, clean application deployment, package validation, database restore and post-restore security checks.</p><div class="os-status-row"><span class="os-chip <?= $verified>0?'good':'' ?>"><?= $verified ?> verified server backup(s)</span><span class="os-chip"><?= backup_step18_h($latest['created_at']??'No backup yet') ?></span><span class="os-chip good">ROLLBACK BEFORE RESTORE</span></div></section><?php if($error):?><div class="pp-alert bad"><strong>Recovery diagnostic:</strong> <?= backup_step18_h($error) ?></div><?php else:?><section class="s10-grid" style="margin-top:14px"><article class="s10-card s10-span-8"><h2>Database / Server Recovery Sequence</h2><div class="s10-list"><div class="s10-row"><div><b>1 • Contain</b><small>Stop writes if corruption or compromise is suspected. Preserve logs and the damaged database before changing anything.</small></div><span class="s10-badge">FIRST</span></div><div class="s10-row"><div><b>2 • Deploy Clean Application Code</b><small>Restore the known-good Healthcare Wellness Club code at the same schema/application version as the recovery package.</small></div></div><div class="s10-row"><div><b>3 • Prepare Empty / Compatible Database</b><small>Run the application migrations until the current schema fingerprint matches the backup package.</small></div></div><div class="s10-row"><div><b>4 • Validate Recovery Package</b><small>Use Restore Center. Authentication, package SHA, organization and schema must pass before apply is enabled.</small></div></div><div class="s10-row"><div><b>5 • Create Pre-Restore Rollback Point</b><small>The restore engine automatically creates an encrypted rollback backup before replacing business data.</small></div></div><div class="s10-row"><div><b>6 • Restore & Re-Authenticate</b><small>Restore revokes all active sessions. Sign in again using credentials contained in the restored backup.</small></div></div><div class="s10-row"><div><b>7 • Run Audits</b><small>Run STEP 10–18 audits, especially Inventory, Purchase, Customer, Finance, Security and Backup audits.</small></div></div><div class="s10-row"><div><b>8 • Reconnect Scheduled / Off-Site Backup</b><small>Scheduler secrets and cloud credentials are environment configuration and are intentionally not restored from the database package.</small></div></div></div></article><aside class="s10-card s10-span-4"><h2>Recovery Evidence</h2><div class="s10-checks"><div class="s10-check <?= $runtime['openssl']?'good':'warn' ?>"><div><b>Encryption Runtime</b><span>AES-256-GCM via OpenSSL</span></div><strong><?= $runtime['openssl']?'PASS':'REVIEW' ?></strong></div><div class="s10-check <?= $runtime['storage_writable']?'good':'warn' ?>"><div><b>Private Backup Storage</b><span>Server package directory</span></div><strong><?= $runtime['storage_writable']?'PASS':'REVIEW' ?></strong></div><div class="s10-check <?= $runtime['staging_writable']?'good':'warn' ?>"><div><b>Private Restore Staging</b><span>Validation workspace</span></div><strong><?= $runtime['staging_writable']?'PASS':'REVIEW' ?></strong></div><div class="s10-check good"><div><b>Passphrase Escrow</b><span>External responsibility; never stored by app</span></div><strong>POLICY</strong></div></div></aside></section><section class="os-card" style="margin-top:14px"><h2>Recovery Scenarios</h2><div class="os-links"><div class="os-link"><div><b>Lost / damaged local PC</b><span>Install XAMPP + project code, prepare database schema, then upload an off-device .hwcbak copy in Restore Center.</span></div></div><div class="os-link"><div><b>Database data corruption</b><span>Take a current evidence backup first, validate the selected older recovery package, then restore with automatic rollback point.</span></div></div><div class="os-link"><div><b>Cloud server migration</b><span>Deploy code/schema first, transfer encrypted .hwcbak over a protected channel, restore, then configure production secrets and HTTPS.</span></div></div><div class="os-link"><div><b>Credential compromise</b><span>Do not blindly restore active sessions. STEP 18 excludes session/login-attempt tables and forces fresh authentication after restore.</span></div></div></div></section><?php endif;?></main></div></body></html>